infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Sizing the heap: two failure modes bracket 1.5–2x live set
  desc Below 1.5x GC thrashes; above 3x you pay for idle memory — target ~1.5–2x the live set
  compares
    - label Undersized
      children
        - label Undersized · below 1.5x
          desc Heap barely larger than the reachable live set
        - label GC runs almost continuously
          desc Too little headroom between cycles, so the pacer keeps re-firing
        - label Marking overhead dominates
          desc Marking cost scales with live bytes and is paid every cycle
        - label Throughput collapses
          desc GC steals the CPU the service needs to serve requests
    - label Oversized
      children
        - label Oversized · above 3x
          desc Heap far larger than the reachable live set
        - label Memory wasted, no latency win
          desc Larger ratios cost RAM without a proportional pause improvement
        - label Each cycle runs longer
          desc More room means more live data may need marking per cycle
        - label Containers charge per-second
          desc Idle headroom is billed continuously in cgroup-limited pods
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b
